                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I ended up enjoying Regency Solitaire way more than I anticipated. It is a solitaire like game where the gameplay is pretty simple to pick up as you have a deck and you try to match cards on the table to the deck. What makes this a bit more unique is that there are also powerups and wild cards to use to help you get through levels. Sometimes to hit an objective, you need to resort to using a lot in a row after saving up, and I definitely ended up doing that quite a bit. As you progress through the levels, there is also a sense of growth as well as you can buy items that improve your powerups or add other slight boosts. I honestly ignored almost all of the story, since I was just itching for a chill solitaire like experience.\r\n\r\nOverall, if you are a fan of Solitaire like games, this one will probably scratch that itch.",
